  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14183030/assets/ad42b4bd62bf64e1ac086a60ace286b3e6d1c136f423d2ae6aabf6339cea9071.png)\n\nWhat length of fence is needed to border a circular plot of land with a diameter of $30\\,\\text{m}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The length of the fence needed to border the circular land is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C=\\pi d,$ where $d=30\\,\\text{m}$ is the diameter.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC=\\pi \\cdot 30=30\\pi \\,\\text{m}.\n$$",
